# Caddy serves the dashboard publicly with automatic HTTPS. DASHBOARD_DOMAIN must be a real
# domain pointing at this server's IP (Caddy then gets a free Let's Encrypt certificate
# automatically). Access control is the platform's OWN login (dashboard/session.py: real
# accounts, scrypt-hashed passwords, lockout, 12-hour sessions) -- there is deliberately no
# Caddy basic_auth here on top of it. A shared basic-auth password was the only protection
# before the platform had accounts of its own; keeping it once real per-user login exists
# would just be a second, club-wide password everyone has to be told, on top of their own
# account -- friction with no security upside. See DEPLOY.md, "Why no Caddy basic-auth".
{$DASHBOARD_DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy dashboard:8501
}
